    "problem_statement": "k_condvar_wait() does not re-acquire the mutex when the wait times out. After a timeout, the mutex is left in an unlocked state, violating the POSIX condition variable contract that requires the mutex to always be held by the calling thread when k_condvar_wait() returns. An application that calls k_mutex_unlock() after a timed-out k_condvar_wait() will get an error because the mutex is not owned by the calling thread.",
